{
 "_doc": [
  "How each form, target and setup string in pairs.tsv becomes script lines. Read by gen_walk.py; see README.md.",
  "Tokens in lines: {S} the spot block (x y z, where the player stands), {T} the target block 2 ahead (+Z),",
  "{B} the side block where a form change leaves the body (3 to +X), {X+dx,dy,dz} an offset from S, T or B,",
  "a C suffix ({SC}, {TC}, {BC}, {TC+0,0,1}) gives the block's bottom centre as decimals,",
  "{NEAR_T} / {NEAR_S} / {NEAR_B} a selector filter for entities within 1.5 blocks of that centre,",
  "{SEL} a selector filter for the whole spot, {LONG X+dx,dy,dz} a block position packed as a long (Tesla Node Target).",
  "Fields: steps (placed before the form change), late (after it), nbt (extra NBT for a generic mob summon),",
  "aim (block | ground | air | [dx, dy, dz] from the T corner), body_at / head_at (T or B), form_steps (replace the form's",
  "own steps), item / offhand (replace the row's), action (use | attack | a whole input line), pre (input lines before",
  "the act marker, e.g. opening a menu), post (after the end marker), bystander (true: the stand-in player is used),",
  "approx (a note: the set-up is close to, not exactly, what the row describes), unreachable (why it cannot be set up).",
  "Merge order: form, then target, then setup, then pairs[id]; later lists are appended, later scalars win."
 ],
